# Staged by fisher-5sg.7 on 2026-11-25.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/,
# fisher-8ie session rules, fisher-r6y D5, D20, D22–D25, D31 and D41,
# fisher-5sg decisions 8 and 10, and expectations/perft.epd.
# python-chess 1.11.2 enumerated legal moves and nodes on 2026-11-25.
# The README beside this transcript records the derivation.
> position startpos
> go movetime 50
# D23/D41 permit reports for finished depths only. At depths 1–4 the
# runner checks D5 by matching the best move to the last reported variation.
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
> stop
> isready
# fisher-8ie rule 4 ignores idle stop. UCI isready requires readyok.
< readyok
> go movetime 0
# D20/D31 require a legal move with no searched report.
< bestmove {legal}
> go movetime 10
# D22/D31 put 10 ms at the same boundary.
< bestmove {legal}

# D23 holds the move even when the time limit ends the search immediately.
> go infinite movetime 0
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# fisher-8ie rule 8 rejects position while a move is held.
< info string {message:position rejected: waiting for stop}
> go movetime 0
# fisher-8ie rule 8 also rejects go while a move is held.
< info string {message:go rejected: waiting for stop}
> isready
# UCI isready and D23 require readyok before release of the held move.
< readyok
> stop
# UCI stop and D24 release the held move.
< bestmove {legal}
> go movetime 0
# fisher-8ie rule 8 preserves the starting position after the rejected commands.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go movetime 0
# D24/D31 accept the new position. Enumeration gives h8h7 as its sole move.
< bestmove h8h7

> quit
# UCI quit requires clean exit with no further output in this idle session.
! exit
